From ffe89a6550acf5f5c3aa791901f90cd5945e77ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 05:40:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 197/211] drm/sun4i: hdmi-phy: Hand out the A733 PLL as a clock

This PLL drives the transmitter and, through the video output top, the
timing controller as well, so describe it as what it is rather than
programming it behind the clock framework's back and leaving the timing
controller pointing at an unrelated CCU clock.

Registering it means creating it at probe rather than from the HDMI
component's bind, since the timing controller binds first and has to find
it. Its parent is the oscillator and its rate comes from a table, so it
never asks the parent for a rate. Several of those entries drive the PLL
in fractional mode, where the integer factors alone do not describe the
result; recalc_rate matches the factors back to the entry carrying them
and reports the rate that entry aims for.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
